  "body": "### Summary\nAs the orchestrator, I want the count-capped polls in the app tests (1 to 5 s budgets in all) to wait on their condition with the shared `until` deadline, so that a loaded macOS runner does not turn them red.\n\n### Scope\n- Examples: `ReaderUnderBarsTests.swift:29` (1 s), `:69` (3 s), `ReaderWebControllerTests.swift:117` (2 s), plus about 20 hosted UI polls of 2 to 5 s. The full list is in PR #1330's body.\n- Replace `for _ in 0..<N where … { sleep }` with `until(…)` or an equivalent deadline helper, one PR per area.\n- Leave the fixed 300–500 ms sleeps before negative checks alone: they cannot fail red.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] No count-capped poll under 30 s remains in `App/SwiftHFRTests`.\n- [ ] Each touched suite is green 10 times under `yes ×4`.\n\nFound by w1324 while fixing #1324 (PR #1330).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
